WEBVTT

00:06.006 --> 00:09.092
[opening theme song playing]

00:45.086 --> 00:47.505
[raindrops pattering]

00:52.594 --> 00:54.596
[somber music]

01:00.226 --> 01:02.228
[hurried footsteps]

01:04.981 --> 01:09.319
[panting]

01:10.278 --> 01:11.488
You're an asshole.

01:12.614 --> 01:13.740
I didn't need to.

01:16.284 --> 01:17.577
[grunts]

01:19.913 --> 01:21.581
I think we should cancel the wedding.

01:25.126 --> 01:27.545
[rain pattering]

01:27.629 --> 01:29.339
[thunder rumbling]

01:35.845 --> 01:36.971
Okay.

01:38.097 --> 01:39.182
"Okay"?

01:42.185 --> 01:43.853
Did you really just say "okay"?

01:45.480 --> 01:48.066
I don't have anything else to say.

01:49.567 --> 01:50.568
"Okay"?

01:50.652 --> 01:52.070
[sobbing]

01:52.153 --> 01:53.196
"Okay"?

01:54.823 --> 01:55.907
"Okay"?

01:56.825 --> 01:57.826
That's it?

01:58.827 --> 02:00.703
"Okay"?
[grunts]

02:01.746 --> 02:02.747
"Okay"?

02:03.665 --> 02:05.708
How could you do this to us?

02:06.459 --> 02:09.295
[sobbing]

02:09.379 --> 02:11.464
[somber music]

02:14.801 --> 02:16.761
[sobbing continues]

02:21.766 --> 02:24.018
[somber music continues]

02:29.399 --> 02:31.109
I'm sorry, Ha-kyung.

02:32.443 --> 02:34.362
You're right. I'm an asshole.

02:35.655 --> 02:39.742
[sobbing]

02:42.620 --> 02:44.414
[rain pattering]

02:45.748 --> 02:48.209
[sobbing]

02:55.758 --> 03:00.763
[thunder rumbling]

03:02.223 --> 03:05.059
The value went up. It went up a lot more.

03:05.143 --> 03:08.021
The apartment was twice
as much as we'd paid for it.

03:09.772 --> 03:12.817
You know I don't have much money on hand.

03:12.901 --> 03:15.445
All of my savings went into that.

03:15.528 --> 03:18.406
[light music playing]

03:20.325 --> 03:21.367
That was your decision.

03:21.451 --> 03:24.579
Well, at first, my wife said
we don't need much,

03:24.662 --> 03:26.456
but that was before we got married.

03:26.539 --> 03:28.750
I'm 36. I'm an adult.
I need to provide for her.

03:28.833 --> 03:30.543
I'm entitled to something, aren't I?

03:33.546 --> 03:37.342
If it really means that much to you,
I'll be fair, halvsies.

03:37.425 --> 03:39.969
You should be so lucky. That's absurd.

03:40.053 --> 03:42.597
It makes sense.
I'm staying at Headquarters.

03:43.181 --> 03:44.182
Why should I care?

03:44.265 --> 03:47.101
Look, I don't want this to turn
into another big fight.

03:47.185 --> 03:48.394
But think about it.

03:48.478 --> 03:50.271
It's better for you
if we don't work together.

03:50.355 --> 03:51.648
- [sighs]
- Am I wrong?

03:52.607 --> 03:56.277
[cell phone buzzing]

03:56.361 --> 03:57.820
[chuckles]

03:59.322 --> 04:01.324
You can take your time and let me know.

04:04.410 --> 04:05.578
Hey, babe.

04:06.663 --> 04:10.208
[Ki-jun chuckles]
No, I went to get you a treat. Macaroons.

04:11.042 --> 04:12.210
On my way back.

04:12.293 --> 04:13.419
[chuckles]

04:16.172 --> 04:19.300
[reporter] You'll want to dress warm
if you're going outside this morning.

04:19.384 --> 04:22.303
The temperature in Gangwon Province
drops below zero.

04:22.387 --> 04:25.765
The temperature in the central region
is also below average for the season.

04:25.848 --> 04:28.559
The weather today
will start a bit like yesterday.

04:28.643 --> 04:33.314
- [indistinct TV chatter]
- [light music]

04:34.816 --> 04:36.818
[sizzling]

04:42.240 --> 04:44.242
[Si-woo] Whether or not we consider
a temperature comfortable

04:44.325 --> 04:45.368
depends on the wind.

04:45.952 --> 04:48.913
The direction of the wind changes
whether we feel warm or cool.

04:48.997 --> 04:51.416
This holds true
even when we're in the same space,

04:51.499 --> 04:52.583
close together.

04:53.876 --> 04:56.337
[Ha-kyung] Excuse me, sir.
Could you turn the heater off, please?

04:57.171 --> 05:00.508
Oh, it's too hot? It's strong, isn't it?
[chuckles]

05:01.342 --> 05:02.510
[chimes]

05:03.928 --> 05:05.263
[remote control thuds]

05:05.346 --> 05:07.140
[knife swooshes, chops]

05:07.849 --> 05:09.809
[Si-woo] Sir, could you turn on
the heater, please?

05:09.892 --> 05:10.810
It's freezing in here.

05:11.561 --> 05:12.478
Huh?

05:14.272 --> 05:15.815
Uh…
[chuckles]

05:15.898 --> 05:16.858
Sure.

05:17.942 --> 05:19.569
[chimes]

05:21.446 --> 05:22.780
[Si-woo] Wind is unreliable.

05:23.364 --> 05:25.116
But the problem is, it's hard to see.

05:25.700 --> 05:27.368
[Ha-kyung] Please, sir.
It's really too hot.

05:28.411 --> 05:29.454
[sighs]

05:30.663 --> 05:31.539
Okay.

05:31.622 --> 05:32.665
[chimes]

05:35.335 --> 05:36.210
[remote control thuds]

05:37.170 --> 05:38.421
[Si-woo] It's too cold in here.

05:38.504 --> 05:39.630
- [knife thuds]
- Damn.

05:41.174 --> 05:42.508
[sighs]

05:43.342 --> 05:47.597
Listen, can you two
just figure this out yourselves?

05:47.680 --> 05:49.307
Whether it stays on or off.

05:50.725 --> 05:52.727
[playful music]

06:02.320 --> 06:03.321
[thuds]

06:05.031 --> 06:07.033
[playful music continues]

06:09.827 --> 06:16.417
EPISODE 2
SENSIBLE TEMPERATURE

06:16.501 --> 06:18.544
[magical music]

06:21.964 --> 06:23.341
[inhales]

06:24.842 --> 06:26.928
She said your ancestors saved you.

06:28.221 --> 06:30.306
Mom, did you see the fortune teller again?

06:30.389 --> 06:31.891
[Tae-kyung] What else did she say?

06:31.974 --> 06:34.185
She said that one day,
you'll be over all this

06:34.268 --> 06:35.728
and be grateful to him,

06:35.812 --> 06:38.856
that you'll say, "Thanks for leaving.
You let me go like that."

06:38.940 --> 06:41.442
You're the one that seems grateful.

06:41.526 --> 06:43.986
I know you never liked him
as a future son-in-law,

06:44.070 --> 06:46.155
so you're relieved he broke it off.

06:46.239 --> 06:47.073
Yeah?

06:47.156 --> 06:49.367
Ha-kyung, our mom is still in shock.

06:49.450 --> 06:51.661
I can't say it's not a little true.

06:51.744 --> 06:53.037
[inhales]

06:54.080 --> 06:56.958
Your dad always wanted to get
to the end of the rainbow with business,

06:57.041 --> 06:57.917
and it was hard on us.

06:58.000 --> 06:59.502
He kept his promises, though.

07:00.378 --> 07:02.421
- Oh, Ma.
- I knew something wasn't right.

07:02.505 --> 07:05.508
Something was off with him
since I first met him.

07:05.591 --> 07:09.053
How can anyone in their right mind
back out of their own wedding

07:09.137 --> 07:10.513
only a month before?

07:10.596 --> 07:11.722
And what a cheapskate.

07:11.806 --> 07:14.600
I know it's normal for a couple
to split the bills these days,

07:14.684 --> 07:17.687
but I've never heard of another bride
who had to pay for so much,

07:17.770 --> 07:18.855
even her own wedding gifts.

07:18.938 --> 07:20.398
Wait. Did you look at my statement?

07:21.149 --> 07:22.316
I didn't even have to.

07:23.609 --> 07:25.445
We used my card, but he paid me back.

07:25.528 --> 07:26.612
Bunch of bull.

07:27.196 --> 07:28.281
[scoffs]

07:29.198 --> 07:30.241
[sighs]

07:31.033 --> 07:33.161
[Mrs. Bae] Enough with the pity party.

07:33.244 --> 07:36.080
When you get the apartment,
make sure you get written proof for it.

07:36.164 --> 07:37.957
That's unnecessary. I own it.

07:38.040 --> 07:41.377
It's very important to get it written out,
or he'll say he's entitled to it.

07:41.461 --> 07:43.504
All right. Calm down, all right?
I'll handle it.

07:43.588 --> 07:45.590
[muttering]

07:47.049 --> 07:49.177
You know that he said
she could have their place

07:49.260 --> 07:51.137
if he was ever to leave her alone.

07:51.220 --> 07:53.764
How can we trust him at all
when he's done worse for less?

08:01.147 --> 08:02.648
JIN HA-KYUNG
KOREA METEOROLOGICAL ADMINISTRATION

08:02.732 --> 08:05.026
[distant children chattering]

08:07.403 --> 08:09.030
[clanks]

08:09.113 --> 08:11.324
[distant vehicle rumbles]

08:16.537 --> 08:18.873
[traffic noise]

08:21.125 --> 08:23.127
[light music]

08:30.259 --> 08:32.678
[wind gusting]

08:38.518 --> 08:40.561
[light music continues]

08:46.275 --> 08:49.278
[wind gusting]

08:52.281 --> 08:55.243
YEOUIDO, SEOUL

08:55.326 --> 08:58.579
SENSIBLE TEMPERATURE 2°C

08:59.372 --> 09:00.373
[car lock beeps]

09:06.546 --> 09:09.340
- [guard 1] What did you say your name was?
- [Si-woo] I'm Lee Si-woo.

09:11.342 --> 09:14.595
Well, I can't let you in
unless you got your station ID card.

09:14.679 --> 09:16.472
I work here, though. I can prove it.

09:17.306 --> 09:19.934
But I left both my ID card
and employee card at home.

09:22.228 --> 09:23.646
[Ha-kyung] Where do I know him from?

09:25.106 --> 09:26.732
[SI-woo] "Si" means time,
"Woo" means rain.

09:26.816 --> 09:29.485
"Rain that come on time." Lee Si-woo.

09:35.866 --> 09:37.577
[guard 1] Here, give me
your employee number.

09:38.452 --> 09:40.037
1835081.

09:40.121 --> 09:42.123
[guard 2] …5081.

09:47.295 --> 09:48.546
That's not you, though.

09:49.255 --> 09:50.756
Well, I…
[chuckles]

09:51.757 --> 09:52.967
I used to be real chubby.

09:53.050 --> 09:55.177
You see, that's when I was studying
for the state exam.

09:55.928 --> 09:56.846
I don't know.

09:57.972 --> 10:00.474
- It's pretty different.
- It is me. I swear.

10:00.558 --> 10:02.685
See, if you look past the fat
here and here.

10:02.768 --> 10:03.936
It's how I look now.

10:04.895 --> 10:06.897
I can confirm that he's an employee.

10:06.981 --> 10:08.524
Oh, you know him?

10:08.608 --> 10:10.318
From the Metropolitan Office.

10:10.943 --> 10:12.194
[guard 1] Oh.

10:13.571 --> 10:15.865
Okay. You can… You can go in.

10:16.490 --> 10:19.160
But talk to HR, see if they can take
a new picture for you.

10:19.243 --> 10:21.370
Okay. Thank you. Goodbye.

10:24.665 --> 10:25.666
Hello again.

10:26.250 --> 10:28.294
Thanks again for helping out back there.

10:28.377 --> 10:30.838
- I appreciate it.
- And it's back to work.

10:35.134 --> 10:36.177
[chuckles]

10:36.260 --> 10:38.346
[indistinct chatter]

10:44.602 --> 10:47.480
- Can I help you?
- Going to work, like you said.

10:49.190 --> 10:50.483
I just got reassigned.

10:50.566 --> 10:52.902
I'm on Severe Weather Forecaster,
Team Two.

10:52.985 --> 10:54.070
What was that?

10:54.153 --> 10:56.614
I'll be here, for two weeks.

10:56.697 --> 10:59.116
[quirky music]

11:04.580 --> 11:06.832
[quirky music continues]

11:08.668 --> 11:10.336
[Bong-chan] Has it been
seven years already?

11:10.419 --> 11:11.671
- [Dong-han] Yes.
- Sir, I need to…

11:11.754 --> 11:13.631
- Yes?
- Oh.

11:14.674 --> 11:17.009
- Good morning.
- I'm glad that you're here.

11:17.760 --> 11:19.387
I wanted to introduce you.

11:19.470 --> 11:21.806
You probably heard from before
that this is Um from Gangneung.

11:21.889 --> 11:25.017
I brought him to be our new
Senior Forecaster on Chief Team Two.

11:25.976 --> 11:26.811
On my team?

11:27.686 --> 11:29.188
- So, Um?
- Yes?

11:29.271 --> 11:32.108
- It'll be great.
- Yeah. I'll do what I can.

11:32.858 --> 11:34.985
It was nice meeting you, Director Jin.

11:35.778 --> 11:39.115
[both chuckle]

11:40.074 --> 11:41.283
Can we talk?

11:44.370 --> 11:45.413
Okay.

11:46.914 --> 11:49.458
You told me to think about it,
but you're forcing me out.

11:51.001 --> 11:52.211
You can stay.

11:53.421 --> 11:56.382
But I do need someone in line if you go.

11:56.465 --> 11:59.051
Soon, we'll have to prepare
for extreme summer weather.

11:59.135 --> 12:00.886
It'll be chaos without a director.

12:00.970 --> 12:02.930
And I can't just bring in someone
off the street.

12:04.056 --> 12:05.766
So I'm ready, just in case.

12:07.768 --> 12:11.230
Also, I know you'll go to Switzerland.
Isn't that why you came in?

12:11.313 --> 12:13.732
No, it's because
of the new severe weather forecaster.

12:14.316 --> 12:15.359
Ah, Lee Si-woo?

12:15.985 --> 12:18.362
That guy is looking for trouble.

12:18.446 --> 12:20.281
Well, first off, he's reckless

12:20.364 --> 12:22.116
and has no respect
for how things are done.

12:22.199 --> 12:24.785
- I know. He's impulsive.
- I'm concerned.

12:24.869 --> 12:27.163
He's got intuition. Like a super power.

12:27.246 --> 12:29.415
We could use
someone like that around here.

12:29.498 --> 12:32.084
Oh, I think he's more trouble
than he's worth.

12:32.168 --> 12:33.627
Please send him to the metro office.

12:36.255 --> 12:38.883
I don't know why you care
who's gonna be on your team

12:38.966 --> 12:41.427
- if you're leaving anyway.
- I never said I was leaving.

12:43.095 --> 12:44.263
So you're staying?

12:46.056 --> 12:48.976
[Ki-jun] Did they tell you
they cancelled my transfer?

12:49.768 --> 12:51.604
Well, I haven't decided yet.

12:54.356 --> 12:55.399
All right.

12:56.233 --> 12:57.401
You have a week. Okay?

12:58.027 --> 13:01.614
You must know how many people applied
to join WMO's program, right?

13:01.697 --> 13:03.824
I need an answer
for the International Division.

13:04.617 --> 13:05.618
One week.

13:06.744 --> 13:07.870
Understood, sir.

13:07.953 --> 13:09.121
[clicks tongue]

13:10.414 --> 13:11.415
[sighs]

13:14.752 --> 13:16.921
- [Myung-ju] You were dispatched here?
- [Si-woo] Uh, yeah.

13:17.004 --> 13:18.797
- [Soo-jin] For how long?
- [Si-woo] Two weeks.

13:19.548 --> 13:20.883
- [Myung-ju] Huh?
- [Soo-jin] What?

13:21.634 --> 13:22.885
Hello there, sir.

13:24.136 --> 13:26.263
Hey, why aren't you
at the Metropolitan Office?

13:26.347 --> 13:27.389
Transfer.

13:28.057 --> 13:31.143
And, hey, why are you here?
You should be at the Gangwon Office.

13:31.977 --> 13:33.354
I've been transferred.

13:33.437 --> 13:34.855
- Oh!
- Really?

13:34.939 --> 13:36.565
Does that mean you're a director?

13:36.649 --> 13:38.526
[Myung-ju] I'm so happy for you.

13:38.609 --> 13:40.986
- I can't believe it took so long.
- Congrats.

13:41.570 --> 13:43.364
Not quite. Not yet.

13:43.948 --> 13:44.865
Which team are you on?

13:45.908 --> 13:48.410
[sighs]
Team Two. Team Two.

13:48.494 --> 13:49.954
- Huh?
- Team Two.

13:50.996 --> 13:52.122
Team Two?

13:52.998 --> 13:55.167
Is this desk okay
for the Senior Forecaster?

13:55.751 --> 13:57.711
Uh, hang on.

13:57.795 --> 14:00.839
You're here as a Senior Forecaster
for Team Two?

14:00.923 --> 14:02.341
Mm-hm. That's right.

14:02.841 --> 14:05.511
And you'll work for Jin Ha-kyung?

14:05.594 --> 14:06.595
[Dong-han] Work?

14:07.638 --> 14:08.764
For her?

14:12.810 --> 14:16.188
NEWS
TRENDING SEARCHES

14:16.272 --> 14:18.065
[chiming]

14:19.358 --> 14:21.360
[soft music]

14:27.116 --> 14:29.493
[soft music continues]

14:35.082 --> 14:36.876
- You're losing your facial fat.
- [chuckles]

14:36.959 --> 14:38.168
It's 'cause you're married.

14:38.252 --> 14:40.087
[all laugh]

14:40.170 --> 14:42.131
[Cho] Do you like it? Being married?

14:42.214 --> 14:43.966
How's Deputy Director Han?

14:44.049 --> 14:45.551
I know he seems he'd be cold and tough,

14:45.634 --> 14:47.303
but he's actually
really sensitive and kind.

14:47.386 --> 14:49.471
- [colleague] Lucky.
- He likes to be helpful too.

14:49.555 --> 14:51.640
He does the chores and he's tidy.

14:51.724 --> 14:52.766
Oh!

14:53.517 --> 14:55.227
I thought he'd be really serious.

14:55.311 --> 14:58.147
Yu-jin, I swear you've been glowing
since the wedding.

14:58.230 --> 14:59.523
- [all chuckle]
- [Cho] Lucky girl.

14:59.607 --> 15:00.691
[colleague] You're so lucky.

15:02.985 --> 15:04.987
[somber music]

15:13.621 --> 15:14.622
[sobs]

15:18.834 --> 15:19.668
[gasps]

15:21.253 --> 15:23.464
[Cho] I feel left out.
I don't want to be single.

15:23.547 --> 15:25.215
I wanna get married now.

15:25.299 --> 15:27.134
I'd see it and I'd catch the bouquet.

15:27.217 --> 15:28.969
- Okay. Mm-hm.
- And then we'll glow too.

15:29.595 --> 15:30.721
[Cho] I wanna be next.

15:30.804 --> 15:31.639
[chuckles]

15:31.722 --> 15:33.766
Okay, fingers crossed. Do it.

15:33.849 --> 15:35.851
But I have to find someone
who'll make me glow too.

15:37.394 --> 15:38.729
Why didn't I say hi?

15:38.812 --> 15:41.148
I made it weird. Why? What did I do?

15:41.231 --> 15:42.232
[employee 1] It's so sad.

15:42.316 --> 15:44.735
[employee 2] Well, that's what happens
if you date a co-worker.

15:44.818 --> 15:47.696
It's great if it actually last,
but you'll probably break up.

15:47.780 --> 15:49.281
It looks stupid for not knowing better.

15:49.365 --> 15:51.784
[employee 1] Well, she found Team Two,
and he's a spokesperson.

15:51.867 --> 15:54.036
It could be worse,
but they'll see each other…

15:54.119 --> 15:55.788
I'd be so sad I'd transfer.

15:55.871 --> 15:58.624
[toilet flushes]

16:00.125 --> 16:01.085
I would too.

16:03.545 --> 16:05.464
- Hello.
- [chuckles]

16:11.804 --> 16:13.806
[quirky music]

16:14.598 --> 16:15.724
[sighs]

16:20.813 --> 16:21.981
[sighs]

16:22.773 --> 16:26.193
It can't be the Siberian air mass,
maybe if it was early in the year.

16:26.276 --> 16:29.446
Still, the Okhotsk Sea air mass
isn't strong enough

16:29.530 --> 16:31.031
to get this far to the west.

16:31.115 --> 16:32.700
Well, with the direction of the wind,

16:32.783 --> 16:34.660
it can only be coming
from the Okhotsk Sea.

16:34.743 --> 16:37.121
Look, maybe if it was born
from the northwest.

16:37.204 --> 16:39.957
Are you saying the sea alone
could drop the temperature this much?

16:40.040 --> 16:41.625
- No way!
- Well, it can't be from Siberian.

16:41.709 --> 16:42.626
What's happening?

16:42.710 --> 16:45.838
They're trying to figure out
why the temperature is going down.

16:45.921 --> 16:48.841
Senior Forecaster Um thinks
it's from the Siberian air mass,

16:48.924 --> 16:51.927
and Forecaster Lee thinks
it's because of the Okhotsk Sea.

16:52.594 --> 16:54.263
We're just scared to intervene.

16:54.346 --> 16:57.433
[Myung-ju] Neither thinks it's possible
for it to be the other air mass.

16:57.516 --> 16:59.143
It's from Siberian. It's Siberian.

16:59.226 --> 17:01.645
The Okhotsk Sea makes more sense
for the time of the year.

17:01.729 --> 17:04.648
Are you considering
the maritime polar air mass?

17:04.732 --> 17:06.650
- You might as well.
- What's that? Is that a joke?

17:06.734 --> 17:08.777
That's impossible.
That's a summertime air mass.

17:08.861 --> 17:10.529
Wouldn't you think
it's just that impossible

17:10.612 --> 17:12.614
that it's 5°C in May?

17:12.698 --> 17:14.867
You're right, but there's no way
it's the maritime polar.

17:14.950 --> 17:17.870
What I'm saying is we need
to consider every single option.

17:17.953 --> 17:19.246
[Ha-kyung] Got it?

17:19.997 --> 17:20.998
Got it?

17:24.084 --> 17:25.836
[footsteps receding]

17:33.135 --> 17:34.094
[sighs]

17:34.178 --> 17:36.138
[comical music]

17:37.765 --> 17:40.184
Am I overreacting, or are you scared too?

17:40.267 --> 17:42.811
The Siberian air mass,
the Okhotsk Sea air mass,

17:42.895 --> 17:44.730
as well as the maritime polar air mass…

17:44.813 --> 17:45.731
[gasps]

17:45.814 --> 17:47.691
And they have no idea what's going on.

17:48.734 --> 17:49.985
Another sign that it's the end.

17:50.861 --> 17:53.864
- You think they might lay everyone off?
- I'm not sure, but…

17:55.741 --> 17:57.910
I don't think Director Jin
will be here for much longer.

17:57.993 --> 17:59.203
- Why?
- Stop that.

17:59.995 --> 18:01.038
If she were,

18:01.830 --> 18:04.792
why would they have transferred Mr. Um
as a Senior Forecaster?

18:04.875 --> 18:08.420
Ah. Is she going to Switzerland?
Someone said that.

18:09.129 --> 18:11.090
- It makes sense now.
- [gasps]

18:11.173 --> 18:12.091
She'd go away?

18:12.174 --> 18:14.968
I heard his transfer was canceled.

18:15.052 --> 18:15.928
Oh, yeah?

18:17.471 --> 18:18.889
So she'd have to see him every day?

18:19.640 --> 18:22.392
That sucks. I'd be so uncomfortable.
Wouldn't you?

18:22.476 --> 18:23.602
[whispering]
For sure.

18:26.063 --> 18:28.398
So now she has to find a way out.

18:28.482 --> 18:30.776
[in normal voice]
That's so unfair. The woman always leaves.

18:30.859 --> 18:32.861
He should go.
He cheated with another woman.

18:33.529 --> 18:36.198
The world doesn't care
about who cheated or who didn't.

18:36.782 --> 18:39.409
It's all about who wants something more,
who has less dignity.

18:40.452 --> 18:44.248
I think she needs to fight a little more
before she goes to start fresh.

18:46.667 --> 18:49.461
Is Director Jin going somewhere?

18:49.545 --> 18:50.754
[clears throat]

18:53.173 --> 18:54.258
It doesn't affect you.

18:54.341 --> 18:57.845
Just do your job,
and go home in two weeks.

18:57.928 --> 18:58.887
Hang on.

18:58.971 --> 19:00.389
[phone rings]

19:01.598 --> 19:04.935
Hello. Team Two.
This is Oh Myung-ju speaking.

19:05.018 --> 19:06.270
[Myung-ju] Uh-huh. Yes.

19:10.107 --> 19:12.109
[somber music]

19:16.572 --> 19:18.574
[footsteps receding]

19:22.786 --> 19:25.122
[somber music continues]

19:30.335 --> 19:31.753
[inhales sharply]

19:35.507 --> 19:36.675
[sighs]

19:40.888 --> 19:42.764
It's like a middle of winter over here.

19:42.848 --> 19:45.017
GANGWON REGIONAL OFFICE
OF METEOROLOGY

19:45.100 --> 19:47.728
Didn't you say the temperature
would warm up again in the evening?

19:47.811 --> 19:48.937
Yes.

19:49.021 --> 19:51.648
[Bong-chan] So, what's happening?
Why is it low?

19:51.732 --> 19:53.734
Based exclusively on the direction
of the wind,

19:53.817 --> 19:56.236
we could say the air mass
in the Okhotsk Sea is causing it.

19:56.320 --> 19:58.405
But we've yet to figure out
why the temperature dropped

19:58.488 --> 19:59.907
- in the first place.
- Really?

19:59.990 --> 20:01.491
What's the current sunlight?

20:01.575 --> 20:03.827
It's 73, similar to the average.

20:03.911 --> 20:05.746
That adds another piece of the puzzle.

20:06.330 --> 20:07.915
- Mr. Um?
- Yes?

20:07.998 --> 20:11.084
- What are your thoughts?
- Oh. Perhaps the remaining cold air

20:11.168 --> 20:14.213
in the northwest found a way to the west.

20:15.923 --> 20:18.050
Like in May of 1978?

20:18.634 --> 20:22.721
This phenomenon could be similar
to the drop we saw in April of 2010.

20:22.804 --> 20:26.266
We determined that the drop was due
to the cold air in the northwest.

20:26.934 --> 20:28.018
All right, but…

20:28.810 --> 20:30.896
what am I seeing over Okhotsk?

20:31.480 --> 20:32.439
We're looking into it.

20:34.733 --> 20:36.360
Of course, that's nothing new.

20:36.443 --> 20:37.444
[Bong-chan clears throat]

20:38.862 --> 20:41.073
Hm? What are your thoughts?

20:41.156 --> 20:43.408
Even if it's just personal opinion
or hunch,

20:43.492 --> 20:45.535
[Dong-han] I think it's sea fog.

20:45.619 --> 20:48.455
It's coming when there's a temperature
difference between air and sea.

20:48.538 --> 20:50.415
The area is also known for it.

20:50.499 --> 20:52.626
[pensive music]

20:57.130 --> 20:58.340
Anyone else have an idea?

21:01.468 --> 21:03.303
All right. Here's the plan.

21:03.387 --> 21:05.597
We tell the media that this is temporary.

21:06.223 --> 21:09.226
Uh, I want you to go down
and explain it to them in person.

21:09.309 --> 21:10.227
Since it is strange…

21:14.815 --> 21:16.650
What? Is something wrong?

21:19.903 --> 21:22.281
- No, sir. It's a good idea.
- Okay.

21:22.364 --> 21:24.157
I'll go now and explain everything.

21:24.241 --> 21:25.242
[exhales]

21:25.325 --> 21:26.243
Mm-hm.

21:26.827 --> 21:29.496
- All right. I'll check in later.
- Yes, sir.

21:29.579 --> 21:31.581
- Thank you, sir.
- Thank you.

21:31.665 --> 21:33.250
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

21:35.335 --> 21:37.379
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

21:42.759 --> 21:44.803
[footsteps receding]

21:48.432 --> 21:50.392
SIMULTANEOUSLY OCCURRING
COLD AND HOT TEMPERATURES IN MAY

21:54.771 --> 21:57.566
We believe the current weather
isn't as simple

21:57.649 --> 21:59.192
as a random irregular season.

21:59.276 --> 22:02.195
We believe it is a consequence
from worldwide climate change.

22:02.279 --> 22:04.239
To manage the mountain climate crisis,

22:04.323 --> 22:06.867
we'll strengthen the communication
and relationship

22:06.950 --> 22:09.911
between our departments in an effort
to protect all from extreme weather.

22:09.995 --> 22:12.122
[Bong-chan] He's good at navigating press.

22:12.205 --> 22:14.875
I think that's why
the Administrator thinks highly of him.

22:14.958 --> 22:16.626
And he wants him to stay close.

22:17.210 --> 22:18.587
He's good with words.

22:18.670 --> 22:19.963
Any questions?

22:20.964 --> 22:22.966
I'm Chae Yu-jin from Munmin Daily.

22:23.050 --> 22:26.219
[reporters murmuring]

22:26.303 --> 22:28.305
[reporters giggling]

22:29.097 --> 22:31.433
How long do you anticipate
the cold is about to last?

22:31.516 --> 22:34.227
For that, I have to defer
to the Chief Forecaster.

22:37.064 --> 22:39.191
[quirky music]

22:40.942 --> 22:43.779
Currently, we see the cold spell
as a brief snap.

22:43.862 --> 22:46.573
It may be cold for another day
or perhaps for two.

22:46.656 --> 22:48.533
So it's gonna get warmer in two days?

22:49.326 --> 22:50.160
We hope so.

22:50.243 --> 22:51.620
According to the data, it's likely.

22:53.371 --> 22:56.750
Well, I hope your prediction is accurate.
I guess we'll see.

22:56.833 --> 22:59.461
Just in case, I'll keep my coat,
'cause you'll never know.

22:59.544 --> 23:01.963
[reporters snickering]

23:02.047 --> 23:03.799
[keyboard clacking]

23:05.550 --> 23:07.135
[inhales]

23:07.219 --> 23:10.347
If there are no more questions,
then this will conclude today's briefing.

23:10.430 --> 23:11.348
[Ki-jun] Thank you all.

23:15.602 --> 23:16.978
[whispers]
Yu-jin!

23:17.479 --> 23:19.022
Wait for me out there in ten.

23:20.649 --> 23:23.193
- Okay.
- Please follow up on that. Thanks.

23:25.445 --> 23:27.280
Congratulations, Director Jin.

23:29.366 --> 23:31.576
[footsteps approaching]

23:32.619 --> 23:34.412
A little bird told me you were promoted.

23:35.122 --> 23:38.375
Wow, so you're the youngest director
in the history of the administration--

23:38.458 --> 23:40.127
Good work, Deputy Director Han.

23:41.086 --> 23:42.712
Have you thought more about the apartment?

23:43.338 --> 23:45.799
What? Why would I need to think about it?

23:46.716 --> 23:49.386
So, Ha-kyung, either way, you win.

23:49.469 --> 23:50.887
Even if we just go halvsies.

23:52.013 --> 23:53.223
But why?

23:53.306 --> 23:54.850
You really love going halvsies, huh?

23:57.686 --> 23:59.396
I wasn't gonna bring it up again, but…

24:00.647 --> 24:03.066
Can you tell me why you took the TV
if it's halvsies?

24:04.234 --> 24:05.402
[sighs]
I told you.

24:05.485 --> 24:07.320
I thought I could take whatever I needed.

24:07.404 --> 24:10.532
And come to think of it,
didn't I pay for the TV myself?

24:10.615 --> 24:12.534
No, you asked
that I'll pay for half of it.

24:12.617 --> 24:13.535
Did I?

24:13.618 --> 24:14.452
[scoffs]

24:14.536 --> 24:16.538
[quirky music]

24:16.621 --> 24:17.539
Oh.

24:18.039 --> 24:21.168
Did we use your card,
'cause I couldn't do it on my card?

24:21.251 --> 24:23.503
Yeah. I wired you 1,240,000 won.

24:23.587 --> 24:25.547
We paid in cash,
so they would install it for us

24:25.630 --> 24:27.632
and give us a toothbrush sterilizer.

24:29.176 --> 24:31.178
Right. I think I recall that.

24:31.261 --> 24:34.264
The TV, induction cooker,
and workout equipment are mine.

24:34.347 --> 24:36.766
If you don't give them back,
the apartment is not considered.

24:36.850 --> 24:38.560
Hey, Jin Ha-kyung, are you serious?

24:38.643 --> 24:40.353
Address me formally and lower your voice.

24:41.062 --> 24:43.231
- This is our workplace.
- Hey.

24:43.732 --> 24:45.192
I told you.

24:45.275 --> 24:47.944
Arguing with you at work
is my worst nightmare.

24:48.028 --> 24:50.071
But if this is how you're gonna be,
you leave me no choice.

24:50.155 --> 24:51.573
You know that's not true.
Do you wanna fight?

24:51.656 --> 24:52.908
- Do you wanna fight?
- Do you wanna fight?

24:52.991 --> 24:54.284
- No, I hate fighting.
- Same here.

24:54.367 --> 24:55.619
[Si-woo] Director Jin,

24:55.702 --> 24:57.454
the Director General asked for you.

24:58.079 --> 24:58.914
[clears throat]

24:59.414 --> 25:01.791
I called you, but your phone
must be turned off.

25:01.875 --> 25:02.709
Oh.

25:05.003 --> 25:06.463
- Let's go.
- Bye.

25:12.260 --> 25:14.429
[footsteps receding]

25:15.889 --> 25:18.683
[pensive music]

25:18.767 --> 25:20.143
[chuckles]

25:24.481 --> 25:25.649
[Ki-jun] Hey, you.

25:28.693 --> 25:29.819
[sighs]

25:31.905 --> 25:33.365
You know who I am, don't you?

25:33.448 --> 25:35.784
- Should I?
- You were at my wedding.

25:36.785 --> 25:37.994
[Ki-jun] Weren't you?

25:38.620 --> 25:40.497
- The bouquet.
- No.

25:43.166 --> 25:44.626
You must think I'm somebody else.

25:46.795 --> 25:48.797
[tense music]

25:51.633 --> 25:53.385
Hey, is everything okay?

25:54.469 --> 25:57.264
Wasn't he that psycho
that tried to wreck the wedding?

25:57.347 --> 26:00.475
Who? That guy?
No, that's absolutely no way.

26:02.060 --> 26:03.270
Are you sure?

26:03.353 --> 26:05.522
[scoffs]
Wouldn't that be wild?

26:05.605 --> 26:08.191
Mm. I've got to go.

26:09.067 --> 26:10.527
- See you back home.
- Mm-hm.

26:23.790 --> 26:25.000
Where are you going?

26:26.042 --> 26:28.211
I thought the Director General
wanted to see me.

26:28.295 --> 26:29.921
I might have made that up.

26:30.005 --> 26:31.798
It seemed like you needed an out.

26:32.465 --> 26:33.383
Ah.

26:34.259 --> 26:38.680
- Um, so, what was happening was--
- I didn't hear or see anything.

26:40.307 --> 26:42.058
That scares me more than saying you did.

26:42.142 --> 26:43.143
[chuckles]

26:43.893 --> 26:45.729
You should get some fresh air.

26:45.812 --> 26:47.105
I'm going back to the office.

26:52.777 --> 26:54.863
[footsteps receding]

26:56.281 --> 26:58.283
[somber music]

27:05.915 --> 27:08.001
[somber music continues]

27:10.378 --> 27:12.380
Can I talk to you in the parking lot?

27:12.464 --> 27:14.382
[footsteps receding]

27:26.978 --> 27:29.481
[somber music]

27:40.575 --> 27:42.911
[somber music continues]

27:46.206 --> 27:48.875
- What are you doing here?
- I work here like you.

27:48.958 --> 27:52.003
You're supposed to be working
at the Metropolitan Office.

27:52.087 --> 27:53.546
I got transferred.

27:53.630 --> 27:54.506
[sighs]

27:54.589 --> 27:55.965
You just have to hurt me more?

27:56.049 --> 27:58.635
Humiliating me at my own wedding
wasn't enough for you?

27:58.718 --> 28:00.261
You followed me. So what's next for you?

28:00.845 --> 28:03.306
I didn't follow you here.
I'm only out here for two weeks.

28:03.390 --> 28:04.391
[scoffs]

28:05.016 --> 28:06.017
[sighs]

28:08.103 --> 28:09.646
So can you keep it together?

28:10.271 --> 28:13.066
Is he gonna lose it if he sees us talking?

28:14.442 --> 28:15.402
I never told him.

28:19.239 --> 28:21.825
I never told him that we lived together.

28:23.159 --> 28:25.453
And I don't think
he'll ever need to know, either.

28:29.416 --> 28:30.250
[scoffs]

28:31.584 --> 28:32.544
[sighs]

28:36.089 --> 28:37.173
[sighs]

28:44.055 --> 28:46.057
[calm music]

28:49.185 --> 28:51.479
[heels clacking]

28:55.608 --> 28:57.819
[whirs]

28:59.571 --> 29:01.823
[calm music continues]

29:09.456 --> 29:12.083
NATIONAL METEOROLOGICAL CENTER
COMPREHENSIVE CONTROL SYSTEM

29:16.546 --> 29:21.801
INNOVATIVE WEATHER SERVICES
A STEPPING STONE TO PUBLIC SAFETY

29:21.885 --> 29:24.345
- Hello.
- Goodbye.

29:25.889 --> 29:28.016
- Oh, hello.
- Hey.

29:28.099 --> 29:29.225
- Hello.
- [door closes]

29:30.310 --> 29:31.478
[sighs]

29:32.061 --> 29:33.980
It's cold out there. Jeez.

29:35.148 --> 29:37.192
You think I don't know?
[sighs]

29:37.275 --> 29:41.070
Look at this. Hm?
The temperature's still going down.

29:42.238 --> 29:44.282
I don't think it's short-term, you know?

29:45.742 --> 29:47.911
- Hello.
- [employee 3] Hello.

29:47.994 --> 29:50.163
Hello. Gosh, it's cold.
[chuckles]

29:51.414 --> 29:52.415
Oh.

29:53.500 --> 29:54.501
[Chief Director] Hey.

29:55.251 --> 29:56.127
Um?

29:56.961 --> 29:58.797
How long has it been, huh?

29:58.880 --> 30:01.466
You see me on the screen every day,
so not that long.

30:01.549 --> 30:04.636
[Chief Director]
You look better on screen.

30:04.719 --> 30:06.304
[men chuckle]

30:06.387 --> 30:07.680
[Chief Director]
I'll let you get back to it.

30:07.764 --> 30:08.598
Thanks.

30:09.516 --> 30:10.892
- Hello.
- [Chief Director] Hello.

30:12.227 --> 30:13.436
Take a look at this.

30:19.275 --> 30:21.277
[quirky music]

30:22.612 --> 30:24.572
[rustling]

30:29.953 --> 30:31.955
[footsteps receding]

30:34.290 --> 30:36.209
[engine revs]

30:46.219 --> 30:47.971
You wanna come get a drink with us?

30:48.054 --> 30:50.682
It's so lucky that we wound up here,
we should get to know you.

30:50.765 --> 30:52.141
Plus, you guys could chat.

30:53.393 --> 30:56.187
Uh, I have to check into my new place
by eight o'clock.

30:56.813 --> 30:57.814
Next time.

31:01.359 --> 31:02.819
I have to go as well.

31:02.902 --> 31:03.945
- Thanks, though.
- Bye.

31:04.028 --> 31:04.904
Goodbye.

31:07.282 --> 31:09.117
Well, I told you they'd say no.

31:10.451 --> 31:12.453
We all know
that acting like a team is key.

31:12.537 --> 31:14.998
It's just that Director Jin
and the new guys,

31:15.081 --> 31:17.333
they all wanna do things their own way.

31:18.835 --> 31:20.920
[engine revs]

31:27.802 --> 31:30.013
Oh, well, it will work out somehow.

31:30.722 --> 31:33.016
We have to focus on the team ourselves.

31:33.099 --> 31:34.767
- So, drinks?
- Mm-hm.

31:34.851 --> 31:36.227
[whimpers]

31:38.396 --> 31:40.565
- It's good?
- Mm, it is.

31:42.942 --> 31:44.193
[doorbell dings]

31:45.278 --> 31:46.112
Who's that?

31:46.863 --> 31:48.573
At this time at night, I don't know.

31:52.368 --> 31:54.746
- Who is it?
- [Dong-han] It's me. Open up.

31:55.788 --> 31:57.332
[lock chimes]

31:57.415 --> 31:58.583
Oh, it's freezing.

31:59.167 --> 32:01.336
It shouldn't be possible in May.

32:01.836 --> 32:03.504
So you're just here all of a sudden?

32:03.588 --> 32:05.131
[sighs]
I told you earlier.

32:05.214 --> 32:07.926
I texted you. I moved to Headquarters
and I'll be home.

32:08.009 --> 32:10.845
- You texted me?
- Oh, come on.

32:11.429 --> 32:12.347
Hello, sir.

32:12.430 --> 32:14.349
[chuckles]
You're so tall now.

32:14.432 --> 32:15.266
[chuckles]

32:19.103 --> 32:20.605
I'm interrupting dinner?

32:21.230 --> 32:23.107
There's not enough. There's no rice left.

32:23.608 --> 32:26.235
That's okay. I ate at the office.

32:26.819 --> 32:28.863
- Please, eat. Eat.
- [mutters]

32:31.240 --> 32:32.241
[sighs]

32:39.540 --> 32:40.959
[exhales deeply]

32:45.797 --> 32:47.382
They assigned you to Headquarters?

32:47.465 --> 32:50.051
Uh-huh, and I'll shift my stuff here.

32:50.551 --> 32:52.303
They should be here tomorrow.

32:52.387 --> 32:55.014
How could you just text
about something so important?

32:55.098 --> 32:57.725
Come on. You know I never liked any fuss.

32:57.809 --> 32:59.268
I…
[gasps]

32:59.352 --> 33:00.228
Gosh.

33:00.311 --> 33:02.897
You needed to have told me
all about this weeks ago.

33:02.981 --> 33:04.691
We don't have space
for your stuff right now.

33:05.984 --> 33:09.195
Well, there isn't… It's not a lot.

33:09.696 --> 33:10.989
It's just two bags.

33:11.072 --> 33:12.740
[grunts]
You're so inconsiderate.

33:13.950 --> 33:14.826
[clatters]

33:16.202 --> 33:18.621
[water sloshing]

33:18.705 --> 33:20.373
- [clatters]
- [inhales]

33:21.791 --> 33:23.418
[slurping]

33:25.378 --> 33:26.879
- [mug thuds]
- [sighs]

33:39.142 --> 33:40.476
[grunts]

33:40.560 --> 33:41.686
That's all, ma'am.

33:42.353 --> 33:44.313
- [Ha-kyung] Thank you so much.
- Have a good day.

33:45.898 --> 33:46.899
You too. Thank you.

33:46.983 --> 33:47.984
- Goodbye.
- Bye.

33:53.406 --> 33:54.699
[lock chimes]

33:55.533 --> 33:56.701
What is this?

33:58.077 --> 33:59.245
[cell phone buzzes]

34:01.539 --> 34:03.750
OFFICE OF SPOKESPERSON
HAN KI-JUN

34:03.833 --> 34:05.001
[Ki-jun] Get everything?

34:06.002 --> 34:08.379
I only took these stuff,
because I thought you wouldn't need it.

34:08.463 --> 34:10.381
- [scoffs]
- You can check. Everything's there.

34:11.007 --> 34:13.634
Oh, please, I wouldn't I need it?
What a joke.

34:13.718 --> 34:16.054
[rustling]

34:16.721 --> 34:18.723
[quirky music]

34:21.309 --> 34:24.187
[camera shutter clicking]

34:24.937 --> 34:26.105
Okay.
[sighs]

34:34.280 --> 34:36.532
[quirky music continues]

34:40.119 --> 34:41.537
NEIGHBORHOOD MARKET

34:41.621 --> 34:43.581
[Ha-kyung] Brand-new TV for sale.

34:54.342 --> 34:55.885
Rice cooker for sale.

34:55.968 --> 34:57.011
[camera shutter clicking]

34:57.095 --> 34:59.388
Speaker for sale. Still in box. 

35:00.098 --> 35:02.225
Suitcases for sale. Unused.

35:04.936 --> 35:05.937
[switch clacks]

35:15.822 --> 35:16.781
[sighs]

35:20.284 --> 35:23.454
Are you sure we're doing right?
I think it's the bottom.

35:23.538 --> 35:24.789
Oh. Oh!

35:25.581 --> 35:27.291
[laughs]
Are you okay?

35:27.375 --> 35:28.584
- It's in your hair.
- Aw.

35:28.668 --> 35:29.961
Ow. Stop it.

35:30.044 --> 35:31.003
[Ha-kyung yelps]

35:31.087 --> 35:32.964
[both laughing]

35:33.047 --> 35:35.591
Hey, if you don't want to do it,
just say so.

35:35.675 --> 35:38.761
- I can't.
- Hey, stop. You're gonna crease it.

35:38.845 --> 35:40.304
It was expensive. Look.

35:40.388 --> 35:42.598
How am I supposed to fix this?

35:42.682 --> 35:44.934
- I think it's lunchtime.
- We're not done.

35:45.017 --> 35:46.519
- I'm hungry.
- [both laugh]

35:47.937 --> 35:49.939
[calm music]

35:52.859 --> 35:54.068
[exhales]

35:56.112 --> 35:57.113
[switch clacks]

35:57.196 --> 35:59.323
[calm music continues]

36:03.244 --> 36:04.620
[lock chimes]

36:05.872 --> 36:07.081
[door closes]

36:08.374 --> 36:09.458
[lock chimes]

36:13.212 --> 36:14.547
[beeps]

36:15.423 --> 36:19.218
YOU RECEIVED A MESSAGE

36:23.723 --> 36:24.640
[sighs]

36:25.850 --> 36:27.768
[buyer] How much for the TV?

36:27.852 --> 36:29.353
[Ha-kyung] Eight hundred thousand.

36:29.437 --> 36:31.898
[buyer] What? How much did you pay for it?

36:33.357 --> 36:34.984
[Ha-kyung] It was 2,480,000 won.

36:35.067 --> 36:37.028
I had it less than three months.

36:37.528 --> 36:40.615
- [buyer] Where did you get it?
- [Ha-kyung] Yongsan Electronics Market.

36:40.698 --> 36:43.326
- [buyer] Come on. You're a scammer.
- What's he saying?

36:43.409 --> 36:44.493
[scoffs]

36:44.577 --> 36:46.746
[Ha-kyung] Excuse me. How am I a scammer?

36:47.663 --> 36:49.916
[buyer] That's an overseas
shipping serial number.

36:50.666 --> 36:51.500
Overseas?

36:51.584 --> 36:52.960
[Ha-kyung] Overseas shipping?

36:53.044 --> 36:54.086
[trills]

36:58.966 --> 37:01.344
[clacking]

37:03.512 --> 37:04.931
[cell phone buzzes]

37:05.014 --> 37:06.057
[whooshes]

37:08.017 --> 37:10.186
[quirky music]

37:12.355 --> 37:13.439
Didn't I pay for the TV myself?

37:13.522 --> 37:15.233
No, you asked
that I'll pay for half of it.

37:15.316 --> 37:18.402
- Did I?
- Yeah. I wired you 1,240,000 won.

37:18.486 --> 37:20.154
AMOUNT I WIRED = 1,240,000 WON

37:20.238 --> 37:21.113
But that's…

37:21.197 --> 37:22.907
[buyer] No one's stupid enough
to fall for this.

37:22.990 --> 37:24.492
Your prices are ridiculous!

37:24.575 --> 37:27.161
[sighs]
Han Ki-jun, you asshole.

37:27.245 --> 37:29.372
[breathes deeply]

37:30.831 --> 37:33.334
[quirky music continues]

37:35.086 --> 37:37.338
[breathes heavily]

37:46.806 --> 37:48.808
[calm music]

37:51.227 --> 37:53.521
[keyboard clacking]

37:59.694 --> 38:01.779
[calm music continues]

38:05.491 --> 38:06.784
No.

38:09.036 --> 38:10.037
[sighs]

38:12.123 --> 38:14.292
[calm music]

38:16.627 --> 38:17.920
[Si-woo] You're here early.

38:19.171 --> 38:22.091
- So are you. Why?
- I just like to do work early.

38:24.969 --> 38:27.680
Ah, Headquarters are so different.

38:27.763 --> 38:29.890
[inhales]
The library's got to be twice as big.

38:29.974 --> 38:31.309
[chuckles]

38:33.769 --> 38:35.938
There's no way you'll finish that
before the meeting.

38:37.690 --> 38:40.484
Unless I help you.
I'll look through these.

38:41.736 --> 38:44.447
Please don't think you're obligated to.

38:45.281 --> 38:46.532
I know that.

38:47.199 --> 38:49.243
Honestly, the Director
didn't even force me to come.

38:49.869 --> 38:50.786
Why are you here?

38:50.870 --> 38:53.706
Wanted to check in, see how you're doing.

38:54.665 --> 38:55.958
Why me?

38:56.542 --> 38:58.002
Well, you two were

38:58.085 --> 39:01.005
all anyone could talk about
when you broke up, right?

39:02.423 --> 39:03.716
So I figured out

39:03.799 --> 39:06.594
that Han Ki-jun was the bastard
that stole my girlfriend,

39:06.677 --> 39:10.264
and that the woman
he was supposed to marry was you.

39:10.348 --> 39:11.515
And I wanted to see you.

39:13.684 --> 39:14.560
[sighs]

39:14.643 --> 39:17.063
This is why you shouldn't date co-workers.

39:18.564 --> 39:20.858
Literally, everyone here knows
about our relationship,

39:20.941 --> 39:22.193
and how it broke down.

39:24.320 --> 39:26.572
What happened when you saw them in person?

39:26.655 --> 39:28.699
It wasn't as bad as I thought it'd be.

39:29.450 --> 39:31.327
- You thought Han Ki-jun--
- How I felt.

39:35.164 --> 39:37.958
I thought my heart would break when I saw.

39:38.042 --> 39:39.627
It actually made me feel better.

39:40.669 --> 39:43.255
Finding out what kind of man she fell for.

39:43.839 --> 39:45.049
It brought clarity.

39:45.132 --> 39:47.385
I get it. He's such a loser.

39:48.094 --> 39:49.804
[chuckles]
Tell me how you really feel.

39:50.638 --> 39:52.515
I really feel like such an idiot, though.

39:52.598 --> 39:55.059
I was in denial
about who he was until he left.

39:57.269 --> 39:58.145
[chuckles]

39:59.522 --> 40:02.608
Switzerland. I hear you're heading out?

40:04.110 --> 40:05.319
Who told you that?

40:06.028 --> 40:08.989
Everyone keeps saying
it's a matter of time before you go.

40:10.241 --> 40:13.077
Honestly, I'm hoping they're all wrong.

40:15.913 --> 40:18.290
Please don't run
just to forget two losers.

40:18.374 --> 40:21.001
[gentle music]

40:25.673 --> 40:28.926
I don't need your counsel,
nor is it your concern.

40:29.635 --> 40:30.928
Like the wind,

40:31.679 --> 40:33.639
an affair might not be visible
in the beginning,

40:33.722 --> 40:35.516
but it will leave a mark
on you personally.

40:36.183 --> 40:38.018
Big or little.

40:44.024 --> 40:46.026
[gentle music continues]

40:52.575 --> 40:54.618
[birds chirping]

40:58.372 --> 41:01.459
[Si-woo] Wow. It's a beautiful morning.

41:03.294 --> 41:05.045
[inhales deeply]

41:05.129 --> 41:06.714
[birds chirping]

41:10.050 --> 41:10.968
What?

41:12.470 --> 41:14.096
You smell that, don't you?

41:15.681 --> 41:17.641
I definitely smell ice in the air.

41:20.060 --> 41:21.228
You can smell ice?

41:22.897 --> 41:24.231
In the last cold wave,

41:24.315 --> 41:26.942
Siberia had it way worse
than we did, you know?

41:27.026 --> 41:29.653
Of course, the sea
was completely frozen over.

41:29.737 --> 41:33.199
What do you think…
happened to all that ice?

41:35.826 --> 41:37.828
[uplifting music]

41:39.580 --> 41:40.748
Let's figure it out.

41:43.042 --> 41:43.876
[chuckles]

41:44.793 --> 41:46.879
[wind howling]

41:46.962 --> 41:49.089
[uplifting music continues]

41:51.842 --> 41:54.428
NAMDAEMUN, SEOUL

41:54.512 --> 41:57.515
SENSIBLE TEMPERATURE 0°C

41:58.599 --> 42:00.726
[Ha-kyung] The cold air
from the sea of Okhotsk

42:00.809 --> 42:02.811
and Sakhalin is flowing to the east.

42:03.938 --> 42:05.606
After examining it this morning,

42:05.689 --> 42:08.734
since it was clear
the sea of Okhotsk had not thawed yet

42:08.817 --> 42:10.402
and froze completely last winter,

42:10.486 --> 42:13.155
it's now chilling the air coming
from the north.

42:13.656 --> 42:16.909
Really? So you're saying
that's ice that's left over?

42:16.992 --> 42:18.285
We believe so, sir.

42:20.496 --> 42:22.706
[uplifting music]

42:26.710 --> 42:28.754
- [wind howling]
- [ice crackling]

42:28.837 --> 42:30.798
[employee 4] So it wasn't sea fog.

42:30.881 --> 42:33.425
[employee 5] It makes sense
since the drop is so dramatic.

42:33.509 --> 42:35.886
- [employee 4] Oh, they did it.
- [employee 5] Oh, man.

42:35.970 --> 42:37.930
[uplifting music continues]

42:41.850 --> 42:43.143
[Bong-chan] No wonder.

42:43.978 --> 42:45.854
What would you say
the water temperature is?

42:45.938 --> 42:48.148
The Kamchatka Peninsula is 5 to 8°C,

42:48.232 --> 42:50.568
and Sakhalin is 3 to 7°C.

42:50.651 --> 42:52.903
Amazing. That's unprecedented. Right?

42:53.404 --> 42:54.780
So what should we do?

42:54.863 --> 42:57.157
To start, we'll record this
as the most unprecedented

42:57.241 --> 42:59.910
and lowest temperature
in the weather observation for May.

42:59.994 --> 43:03.205
We should announce the prediction
that the weather in Taebaek and Bonghwa

43:03.289 --> 43:06.875
and Gyeongbuk down
to as much as .5 and 1.2°C respectively.

43:06.959 --> 43:09.169
Unprecedented and lowest. Hmm…

43:09.253 --> 43:11.088
- Okay. Let's do it.
- [Ha-kyung] Yes, sir.

43:11.171 --> 43:12.214
Of course, it's ice.

43:12.298 --> 43:13.757
[Bong-chan] All right, going forward,

43:13.841 --> 43:16.427
I wanna know how long
this will last, approximately.

43:16.510 --> 43:17.678
[chuckles]

43:20.723 --> 43:22.057
[Si-woo] Are you going to lunch?

43:23.017 --> 43:25.227
- What if I am?
- Then I'll go too.

43:26.895 --> 43:28.022
Uh, Mr. Lee.

43:28.731 --> 43:30.774
Go to the cafeteria
or should we treat ourselves?

43:31.650 --> 43:34.528
- You really knew it was ice?
- Huh?

43:36.030 --> 43:38.449
You smelled it. Ice in the air?

43:38.532 --> 43:41.744
How can you smell ice
all the way from the seas of Okhotsk?

43:41.827 --> 43:43.495
I wouldn't think that it's possible.

43:44.538 --> 43:45.706
[chuckles]

43:47.082 --> 43:48.709
I'm only human.

43:48.792 --> 43:50.085
How could I have smelled ice?

43:50.169 --> 43:52.880
I don't even think
a dog could from so far away.

43:54.006 --> 43:55.549
Then what were you saying earlier.

43:56.550 --> 43:59.178
I found out by reading in the library.

44:07.227 --> 44:09.188
[clicking]

44:11.690 --> 44:12.900
[inhales]

44:19.156 --> 44:20.324
[keyboard clacks]

44:20.949 --> 44:22.409
[inhales]

44:26.288 --> 44:27.456
[scoffs]

44:28.290 --> 44:30.292
[lively music]

44:30.376 --> 44:34.213
[groaning]

44:37.591 --> 44:39.551
[footsteps receding]

44:51.980 --> 44:54.316
[lively music]

44:58.445 --> 44:59.405
[clacks]

45:01.448 --> 45:03.450
[lively music continues]

45:14.294 --> 45:15.712
[exhales heavily]

45:30.352 --> 45:31.812
[keyboard clacking]

45:34.815 --> 45:37.151
[lively music]

45:47.202 --> 45:48.412
You're here early.

45:49.997 --> 45:51.248
So are you. Why?

45:51.874 --> 45:53.876
I just like to do work early.

45:55.669 --> 45:57.337
[phone buzzing]

45:58.046 --> 46:00.257
- You're more gullible than you look.
- [cell phone buzzing]

46:00.340 --> 46:01.633
- Tae-kyung.
- [Tae-kyung] Ha-kyung.

46:01.717 --> 46:03.719
I thought you said
you'd take care of the apartment?

46:03.802 --> 46:04.636
Oh, what happened?

46:04.720 --> 46:07.222
A certified delivery receipt
came today for you.

46:07.306 --> 46:08.932
What? Is it that bad?

46:09.016 --> 46:09.850
[Tae-kyung sighs]

46:09.933 --> 46:12.186
Does Han Ki-jun think we can't see
what he's doing to you?

46:12.269 --> 46:13.604
He wants your apartment!

46:13.687 --> 46:15.731
[quirky music]

46:16.648 --> 46:18.775
And Ma has never been this mad before.

46:18.859 --> 46:20.152
She said she wants to find him

46:20.235 --> 46:21.904
and see if a beating
would set him straight.

46:21.987 --> 46:24.072
I'm trying to hold her back,
so she doesn't go crazy

46:24.156 --> 46:25.532
at your work, you know?

46:27.451 --> 46:29.369
- Are you there?
- [rustling]

46:29.453 --> 46:32.039
Hey, Ha-kyung. Ugh, shit.

46:32.122 --> 46:34.208
[quirky music continues]

46:44.218 --> 46:45.177
Han Ki-jun!

46:46.512 --> 46:47.554
Come here.

46:48.639 --> 46:49.765
[door slams]

46:54.520 --> 46:55.896
She wants you to go.

47:03.779 --> 47:04.738
[grunts]

47:06.615 --> 47:08.784
What the hell was that for?

47:11.495 --> 47:13.372
Listen. We're at work.

47:14.206 --> 47:15.624
You're worried about all the gossip?

47:15.707 --> 47:17.668
Then maybe you shouldn't be
messing with me.

47:17.751 --> 47:19.002
What did I do?

47:19.086 --> 47:20.837
You're making it look like
I owe you something.

47:20.921 --> 47:23.048
How dare you? After everything else.

47:23.131 --> 47:24.800
Or did you forget we were together?

47:24.883 --> 47:27.135
What happened is completely separate
from the apartment.

47:28.303 --> 47:29.972
You're not even sorry, are you?

47:30.639 --> 47:31.932
I said that I was.

47:32.015 --> 47:33.433
How many times do I have to say it?

47:33.517 --> 47:34.560
More than once.

47:35.852 --> 47:38.188
You said you're sorry once,
then you started to pack.

47:38.272 --> 47:39.856
I did say it, though.

47:43.151 --> 47:47.030
Yeah. After we've spent
ten years together.

47:47.114 --> 47:48.156
Ten years.

47:48.240 --> 47:50.409
Then you decided
you didn't want that anymore.

47:51.285 --> 47:54.413
So fine. You said you couldn't help it,
it was my fault, so…

47:54.913 --> 47:56.999
Even if that's so,
you could've really apologized

47:57.082 --> 47:59.042
instead of mumbling while you left.

47:59.126 --> 48:02.337
You're the one who said
I should consider the apartment alimony.

48:02.421 --> 48:05.591
Why? Because you wanted it
to be over ASAP, is that right?

48:08.051 --> 48:11.138
Anyway, I thought it was my fault.

48:11.221 --> 48:12.973
You were just reacting to the situation.

48:13.056 --> 48:14.850
I've been stressed
and too focused on work.

48:14.933 --> 48:16.310
It was my fault for not doing more.

48:16.393 --> 48:19.479
And if I paid more attention,
I would've seen how lonely you were.

48:19.563 --> 48:21.815
I thought that if I'd put more
into the relationship--

48:21.898 --> 48:24.151
- Why say it if we both know?
- We do?

48:25.444 --> 48:28.071
You're right. We spent ten years together.

48:28.572 --> 48:31.867
Do you have any idea for those ten years
how unhappy I was?

48:31.950 --> 48:34.369
You thought I was worthless,
because you outranked me.

48:34.453 --> 48:35.579
You'd always say,

48:35.662 --> 48:39.124
"Deputy Director Han, bring me water.
Coffee. Get me a snack."

48:39.207 --> 48:41.376
You thought I spent all my time
just waiting for you.

48:41.460 --> 48:43.170
And the wallpaper in the apartment.

48:43.253 --> 48:44.921
We could have just hired someone to do it,

48:45.005 --> 48:48.425
but you insist that we do it together,
and I missed my day at work.

48:48.508 --> 48:50.177
Do you remember how that ended?

48:50.260 --> 48:53.639
They called you into work,
so I had to do the rest of it alone.

48:54.890 --> 48:55.974
I…

48:56.058 --> 48:58.477
I was so exhausted at the end of the day.

48:59.186 --> 49:01.063
Then you should have said something to me!

49:01.146 --> 49:02.105
Say something?

49:02.606 --> 49:04.232
You would've sulked until I let it go.

49:05.567 --> 49:06.610
When I think about it now,

49:06.693 --> 49:08.570
how I felt like
I had to prove myself to you,

49:08.654 --> 49:10.405
I can't believe I accepted it.

49:10.489 --> 49:11.948
And you had no idea, did you?

49:14.159 --> 49:15.702
[breathes sharply]

49:15.786 --> 49:16.745
[sobs]

49:17.371 --> 49:18.789
So that means that

49:19.915 --> 49:22.209
all those years meant nothing to you?

49:23.210 --> 49:24.419
Whatever.

49:25.212 --> 49:26.963
How much will you give me
for the apartment?

49:27.047 --> 49:29.091
You said it yourself,
do ten years mean nothing?

49:29.174 --> 49:32.052
It's selfish for you to keep it
to yourself, you know that.

49:32.135 --> 49:34.179
[dramatic music]

49:34.262 --> 49:35.389
[inhales]

49:36.181 --> 49:37.557
It's been sold.

49:38.725 --> 49:41.269
You sold it? Really?

49:41.353 --> 49:43.980
We signed a contract,
they'll pay by the end of the month.

49:44.690 --> 49:46.191
So how much am I getting from that?

49:46.858 --> 49:49.653
It cost us 20 million won,
and you deposited 5.

49:49.736 --> 49:51.279
I paid the rest on my own.

49:51.363 --> 49:55.033
But I also covered the deposit,
down payment, and the mortgage on my own.

49:55.701 --> 49:58.203
So… So what are we going to get?

49:58.286 --> 50:01.164
Could we say that you only own 7%?

50:02.332 --> 50:04.918
And then I have to deduct
all the money that you stole from me

50:05.001 --> 50:07.462
when you said I was paying half
for things you got overseas.

50:07.546 --> 50:08.672
Wire it to you.

50:08.755 --> 50:10.257
Wait, Ha-kyung, I--

50:10.340 --> 50:14.803
Halvsies? You must be joking.
That's low, even for you.

50:15.887 --> 50:18.515
You're moving.
You're going to Switzerland, aren't you?

50:18.598 --> 50:20.392
You can back out. Give it to me.
'Cause you don't need it.

50:20.475 --> 50:22.102
Who says I'm going to Switzerland?

50:22.185 --> 50:23.729
Everyone thought that…

50:24.354 --> 50:25.230
You're staying here?

50:25.313 --> 50:27.315
[scoffs]
I'm the youngest director in history.

50:27.399 --> 50:28.358
Why will I leave that?

50:28.442 --> 50:30.694
Oh, won't you hate seeing me
like this every single day?

50:30.777 --> 50:32.529
Oh, is it hard for you to see me?

50:32.612 --> 50:34.364
It's sounds like
you're the one who should go.

50:34.448 --> 50:37.159
I think you should be in Geneva,
you asshole!

50:39.035 --> 50:42.831
[all murmuring]

50:43.749 --> 50:45.917
[dramatic music]

50:47.586 --> 50:49.546
I don't want to hear about this.

50:49.629 --> 50:50.881
Ever again.

50:50.964 --> 50:52.966
[upbeat music]

50:57.596 --> 50:59.097
The show's over.

51:02.350 --> 51:04.728
[upbeat music continues]

51:07.606 --> 51:08.857
Sir, Switzerland is off.

51:10.358 --> 51:12.402
Seriously? You're staying?

51:13.028 --> 51:15.363
Yes. I'm going to get
Chief Team Two into shape.

51:16.406 --> 51:18.450
Okay. Then let's celebrate.

51:18.533 --> 51:21.995
I'm sorry, I have to get home.
We have lots to do tomorrow. Thank you.

51:24.164 --> 51:26.291
[upbeat music]

51:31.421 --> 51:32.672
[chuckles]

51:32.756 --> 51:33.757
[music stops]

51:39.930 --> 51:41.014
[sighs]

51:45.560 --> 51:47.938
[engine revs]

51:50.649 --> 51:51.900
[Si-woo] Director Jin.

51:52.984 --> 51:55.278
- Can I help you?
- Do you wanna get a drink?

51:57.697 --> 52:00.075
I know a great spot,
and it's not too far from here.

52:02.953 --> 52:04.955
[playful music]

52:11.628 --> 52:13.713
- Enjoy.
- Thank you.

52:20.554 --> 52:21.471
Cheers.

52:22.305 --> 52:24.099
- [both chuckle]
- [door closes]

52:25.809 --> 52:29.354
I'm not used to drinking
with other people around.

52:31.439 --> 52:32.357
Really?

52:34.317 --> 52:36.945
I know. You met him at a bar, didn't you?

52:37.821 --> 52:39.322
Is that what you think of me?

52:39.406 --> 52:41.491
We've been dating
since we were in college.

52:41.575 --> 52:43.702
Then we both got in to the same office.

52:43.785 --> 52:45.036
Oh.
[sighs]

52:45.120 --> 52:49.082
My co-workers who'd been there a while
said not to date any co-workers.

52:49.666 --> 52:52.043
So Ki-jun and I kept it a secret.

52:52.627 --> 52:54.337
But at the welcome party,

52:54.421 --> 52:58.049
I drank too much
and shouted at everyone that he was mine.

52:58.133 --> 53:00.343
- [chuckles]
- The rest is history.

53:01.970 --> 53:04.389
- What about you?
- Huh?

53:04.472 --> 53:05.932
The bouquet, what happened?

53:06.975 --> 53:08.018
Oh.

53:09.644 --> 53:10.562
About that.

53:10.645 --> 53:12.188
[quirky music]

53:12.856 --> 53:14.232
[photographer] Yeah. One last photo.

53:14.316 --> 53:15.817
Smile, everyone!

53:15.901 --> 53:19.696
All right. One, two, three.

53:19.779 --> 53:20.780
[camera shutter clicks]

53:20.864 --> 53:23.033
[photographer] Next is the bouquet toss.

53:23.116 --> 53:26.286
[applause]

53:32.834 --> 53:35.170
[tense music]

53:46.932 --> 53:48.516
[Si-woo] And I ran as fast as I could.

53:48.600 --> 53:50.352
[gasps]
You got away with it?

53:50.936 --> 53:53.229
Well, if some guys are
out there stealing girlfriends,

53:53.313 --> 53:54.314
that was nothing.

53:55.065 --> 53:58.026
Oh, you're completely insane.
But I'll drink to that.

53:58.693 --> 53:59.778
Cheers!

54:01.947 --> 54:02.864
[sighs]

54:02.948 --> 54:04.199
[exhales]

54:06.451 --> 54:08.954
I'd say Yu-jin was my first real love.

54:09.913 --> 54:10.997
But you know what?

54:11.498 --> 54:14.000
After messing with her to get revenge,

54:14.584 --> 54:16.044
I'm letting her go.

54:16.127 --> 54:17.212
[clinks]

54:18.797 --> 54:20.340
I got to tell you.

54:20.423 --> 54:23.510
Yu-jin's hands
are straight up cursed for real.

54:23.593 --> 54:24.970
Cursed?

54:25.053 --> 54:26.805
If she picked it, it's wrong.

54:26.888 --> 54:27.973
You know?

54:28.056 --> 54:31.184
So I was thinking that could be
the real reason

54:31.267 --> 54:32.519
she chose him over me.

54:33.144 --> 54:34.354
It may be.

54:34.938 --> 54:37.399
Han Ki-jun is really childlike.

54:37.482 --> 54:41.111
If he gets a cold,
he'll whine until the whole world knows.

54:41.194 --> 54:42.779
[gasps]
Maybe she's into that.

54:42.862 --> 54:44.114
[chuckles]

54:44.197 --> 54:45.490
I can take care of myself.

54:45.573 --> 54:47.075
He's an awful driver too.

54:47.158 --> 54:49.744
It took him, like, five tries
to get his license.

54:49.828 --> 54:51.079
I got it on my first try.

54:51.162 --> 54:53.373
Really? Here.

54:53.456 --> 54:54.916
- Cheers.
- Cheers.

54:55.000 --> 54:56.418
[exhales sharply]

54:58.545 --> 54:59.796
And he's self-obsessed.

54:59.879 --> 55:02.882
It'd take him an hour to get an outfit,
so he's always late.

55:02.966 --> 55:04.384
Oh, and he hates bugs.

55:04.467 --> 55:05.760
He can't handle spicy food.

55:06.302 --> 55:08.763
And of course, he is so, so cheap.

55:08.847 --> 55:11.808
You heard that, though,
him asking me how much money he'd get?

55:11.891 --> 55:12.851
[scoffs]

55:19.899 --> 55:21.609
[breathes deeply]

55:22.277 --> 55:25.321
What was it about him
that made you wanna marry him?

55:28.408 --> 55:29.617
Uh…

55:31.494 --> 55:34.080
Well… Hmm…

55:36.124 --> 55:38.209
I guess I didn't mind the bad stuff.

55:39.711 --> 55:43.256
I didn't care that he needed
to be babied when he got a cold.

55:45.383 --> 55:48.511
I liked that he was frugal,
'cause it made me feel safe.

55:49.137 --> 55:50.597
'Cause he was looking out for us.

55:53.308 --> 55:54.392
Most of all,

55:55.477 --> 55:58.229
he was extremely proud of me
on what I did.

55:59.189 --> 56:01.232
[light music]

56:02.609 --> 56:04.694
I guess I was wrong about all of that.

56:08.364 --> 56:11.034
[light music continues]

56:12.368 --> 56:14.621
At least I know who he really is now.

56:15.663 --> 56:17.957
- Oh, really?
- Wind.

56:18.666 --> 56:19.584
What?

56:19.667 --> 56:22.712
You said wind always leaves a mark
even if we don't see it right away.

56:22.796 --> 56:23.671
[chuckles]

56:23.755 --> 56:26.341
I couldn't see the wind
or what it was doing to me.

56:27.300 --> 56:30.220
Then recently, I did see, so I'm done.

56:32.972 --> 56:34.349
Thanks for all that.

56:37.977 --> 56:39.437
Just happy I could help.

56:40.355 --> 56:41.481
[chuckles]

56:42.023 --> 56:44.651
[food sizzling]

56:46.653 --> 56:48.154
Isn't it warm in here?

56:49.239 --> 56:50.490
[Si-woo] Yeah, you're right.

56:50.990 --> 56:53.618
- It is warm in here.
- [chuckles]

56:53.701 --> 56:56.162
You… You're both too warm, you sure?

56:56.246 --> 56:57.622
Yes.
[chuckles]

57:00.667 --> 57:01.876
[chimes]

57:03.878 --> 57:06.297
- Should we get another bottle?
- I'd love to.

57:06.381 --> 57:08.049
Excuse me, can we get another?

57:08.133 --> 57:09.300
[restaurant owner] Of course.

57:11.386 --> 57:14.597
[Ha-kyung] Ugh, I'll never date
a co-worker ever again.

57:14.681 --> 57:17.308
[Si-woo] Really? "Never" is a strong word.

57:17.934 --> 57:22.397
[Ha-kyung] I know. I'm never going to date
anyone I work with ever again.

57:23.940 --> 57:26.693
[Si-woo scoffs]
Thank you.

57:29.320 --> 57:30.738
[rattling]

57:32.323 --> 57:34.367
You sure you didn't see
the signs of the ice?

57:34.951 --> 57:36.995
Even now, when I look, I just see fog.

57:38.204 --> 57:41.708
Director Jin and Si-woo,
they, they found it on their own.

57:41.791 --> 57:43.042
Noted.

57:44.294 --> 57:46.796
You act tough, but you're a tsundere,
soft on the inside.

57:46.880 --> 57:48.756
Well, I'll still beat you.

57:48.840 --> 57:51.009
Wait. I didn't see that. Give me a second.

57:51.509 --> 57:54.304
[inhales]
How did I miss that? Over.

57:54.387 --> 57:55.597
[inhales sharply]

57:55.680 --> 57:56.973
[laughs]

57:57.056 --> 57:58.975
I don't get it. You're happy to lose?

57:59.601 --> 58:01.019
Huh?
[inhales]

58:01.102 --> 58:04.689
Not that, it's just, it's just that
Jin said she's going to stay for a while.

58:05.648 --> 58:08.902
And she wants to keep leading
and to run Team Two.

58:09.527 --> 58:11.696
Um, I see.

58:11.779 --> 58:13.990
[inhales]
Which is difficult.

58:14.574 --> 58:18.703
'Cause you'd have to wait longer
before I make you a director.

58:18.786 --> 58:23.166
I told you, I don't need to be a director,
that's not why I'm here, it's all right.

58:25.585 --> 58:28.004
Knowing Team Two,
you'll have your hands full.

58:28.087 --> 58:29.589
[both laugh]

58:33.676 --> 58:34.969
[sighs]

58:35.053 --> 58:37.472
Darn it. I don't care.

58:37.555 --> 58:39.516
[chuckles]

58:47.398 --> 58:48.983
[distant indistinct chatter]

58:58.826 --> 59:00.828
[quirky music]

59:14.425 --> 59:17.512
[quirky music continues]

59:24.060 --> 59:25.228
You awake?

59:25.728 --> 59:27.647
[groans]

59:29.482 --> 59:30.483
[sighs]

59:41.202 --> 59:43.413
[music fades]

59:57.176 --> 59:58.303
Sorry.

59:59.887 --> 01:00:00.722
What?

01:00:01.973 --> 01:00:05.059
I have to apologize
for what happened last night.

01:00:07.103 --> 01:00:10.023
I thought we were both on board.

01:00:13.026 --> 01:00:15.570
And it was good.

01:00:15.653 --> 01:00:17.572
[quirky music]

01:00:18.281 --> 01:00:19.991
- Have a good night.
- Goodbye.

01:00:20.575 --> 01:00:23.036
Hey, Si meaning time,
Woo meaning rain, you rock.

01:00:24.037 --> 01:00:25.246
For real?

01:00:25.330 --> 01:00:28.416
If me being so big,
you think can I kiss you?

01:00:29.542 --> 01:00:31.878
[both laugh]

01:00:31.961 --> 01:00:34.589
- You won't.
- I will. See?

01:00:45.266 --> 01:00:47.268
[romantic music]

01:00:59.405 --> 01:01:01.699
[romantic music continues]

01:01:15.380 --> 01:01:17.465
[romantic music]

01:01:22.637 --> 01:01:23.805
[music fades]

01:01:26.057 --> 01:01:27.100
[sighs]

01:01:28.226 --> 01:01:30.228
[playful music]

01:01:31.854 --> 01:01:33.856
You're right. We're both adults, you know?

01:01:33.940 --> 01:01:34.941
That's true.

01:01:36.734 --> 01:01:38.319
So what happened,

01:01:39.237 --> 01:01:41.030
it was only a hookup.

01:01:41.114 --> 01:01:43.282
It shouldn't have happened, but it did.

01:01:43.366 --> 01:01:45.493
It's more like a natural disaster.

01:01:45.576 --> 01:01:48.538
Like when two air currents
that shouldn't meet, do,

01:01:48.621 --> 01:01:51.165
and wind up creating lightning, you know?

01:01:51.249 --> 01:01:52.291
Okay. So?

01:01:53.292 --> 01:01:55.086
I think we have to…

01:01:57.171 --> 01:01:59.048
[breathes heavily]

01:02:00.341 --> 01:02:01.718
We have to forget all this,

01:02:01.801 --> 01:02:03.886
and move on like adults.

01:02:06.848 --> 01:02:10.727
It makes sense that you're going back
to the Metropolitan Office next week.

01:02:10.810 --> 01:02:13.312
And I need to focus on managing Team Two.

01:02:13.396 --> 01:02:15.481
So I really don't need any distraction.

01:02:15.565 --> 01:02:17.900
I honestly don't have time
for anything else.

01:02:17.984 --> 01:02:19.485
And you're my co-worker.

01:02:19.569 --> 01:02:21.904
I can't do that. You understand, right?

01:02:21.988 --> 01:02:23.322
No, yeah, I do.

01:02:23.406 --> 01:02:24.615
[both chuckle]

01:02:25.533 --> 01:02:27.577
Okay. Well, it's good that we agreed.

01:02:27.660 --> 01:02:29.203
- Yeah.
- [chuckles]

01:02:29.287 --> 01:02:30.872
- Good work.
- Thanks.

01:02:32.582 --> 01:02:34.208
[both chuckle]

01:02:35.543 --> 01:02:36.711
All right, then.

01:02:36.794 --> 01:02:37.795
[awkward chuckle]

01:02:38.629 --> 01:02:39.922
By the way…

01:02:41.215 --> 01:02:42.300
I'm not leaving, either.

01:02:45.303 --> 01:02:46.262
Hm?

01:02:46.345 --> 01:02:50.308
They said I've been officially made part
of Team Two,

01:02:51.142 --> 01:02:52.769
it formally starts next week.

01:02:56.856 --> 01:02:57.899
What did you say?

01:02:58.483 --> 01:03:00.443
I'm with you, we're on the same team now.

01:03:01.235 --> 01:03:03.446
[dramatic music]

01:03:09.368 --> 01:03:11.037
That won't make things difficult.

01:03:11.120 --> 01:03:14.248
And we'll move on, like adults.

01:03:16.375 --> 01:03:17.418
Okay.

01:03:17.502 --> 01:03:19.504
[upbeat music]

01:03:31.474 --> 01:03:34.310
[water trickling]

01:03:36.854 --> 01:03:38.064
[music stops]

01:03:41.317 --> 01:03:42.944
This is insane.

01:03:43.528 --> 01:03:45.947
[closing theme music]

01:04:11.055 --> 01:04:13.766
Where is Director Jin?
Is she always this late?

01:04:14.851 --> 01:04:16.102
[gasps]

01:04:16.185 --> 01:04:17.436
Satellite center…
[sneezes]

01:04:18.187 --> 01:04:21.482
[fisherman] Please lift the fishing ban.
What are you doing?

01:04:21.566 --> 01:04:23.651
Ugh. We're doing our best
to keep you safe.

01:04:23.734 --> 01:04:25.444
When there's severe weather,

01:04:25.528 --> 01:04:28.406
if we mess it up, it leads to casualty,
don't you know that?

01:04:28.489 --> 01:04:30.449
You're drawing things out on purpose.

01:04:30.533 --> 01:04:32.493
You're letting your feelings
affect your judgement.

01:04:33.077 --> 01:04:36.330
[Si-woo] Don't worry. I won't ask you out
just because we hooked up.

01:04:36.414 --> 01:04:38.082
- Cool.
- [Ha-kyung] They're gonna see us!

01:04:38.958 --> 01:04:42.044
[Si-woo] Oh, no. Why are you acting guilty
if there's nothing to hide?

01:04:43.379 --> 01:04:44.881
That was too close.

01:04:44.964 --> 01:04:46.757
Do you have feelings for me?
